    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d668">

                <pb facs="0611" n="495" xml:id="pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857 T53/31.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Consul General at Halifax</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 24, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There are no restrictions as far as the United States quarantine regulations are
                    concerned if the bodies are embalmed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
